  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I couldn't find a past ticket reporting this problem. None of the archived tickets covers `wslc image import` failing with E_INVALIDARG when the image name has no tag. The closest ones are different problems. WSL#40944 is a wslc E_INVALIDARG caused by a Windows username containing a '.', and it affects every wslc command, not just import. The other import tickets are about `wsl --import` of distro tarballs. As a workaround, specify the tag explicitly, for example `wslc image import alp.tar test:latest`, which you've confirmed works. This looks like a new bug, so it needs a fresh report: wslc should default to :latest when no tag is given, as docker does.\"}",
